{"requirements":[{"id":"R1","requirement":"Restore the supplied export into the branch_orders database on node1 while preserving supplied primary keys, customer/order relationships, and exact monetary values.","status":"satisfied","summary":"The final database contains the two supplied customers and three supplied orders with the original IDs and amounts. Both primary keys, the customer foreign key, DECIMAL(10,2), and zero orphan orders were directly verified.","evidence_ids":["cmd-7088cda3f906435e","cmd-14f5dfd4da344d01","cmd-d80c53a6f823417b","cmd-3a3f13e99c764489"]},{"id":"R2","requirement":"Provide a reporting account that can read customers and orders from node2 but cannot modify them.","status":"satisfied","summary":"Node2 successfully read and joined both tables. The account has only table-level SELECT grants; an INSERT into customers and an UPDATE to orders were denied, with the checked data remaining unchanged.","evidence_ids":["cmd-a91520baa9e24ea0","cmd-6756b3ec411a48e7","cmd-f4bd6b3e818340ed","cmd-3a3f13e99c764489"]},{"id":"R3","requirement":"Ensure the database administrator retains write access.","status":"satisfied","summary":"The branch_dba account has database-wide privileges. Transactional customer/order inserts succeeded and were rolled back, directly demonstrating write capability without changing final data.","evidence_ids":["cmd-d80c53a6f823417b","cmd-3a3f13e99c764489"]},{"id":"R4","requirement":"Preserve the supplied SQL export.","status":"satisfied","summary":"The export retained its baseline 452-byte size and SHA-256 hash through import, restart, and final verification.","evidence_ids":["seeded-state-node1","cmd-7088cda3f906435e","cmd-14f5dfd4da344d01","cmd-9accce7701e64cae","cmd-3a3f13e99c764489"]},{"id":"R5","requirement":"Keep the installed operating-system release and kernel and use software compatible with the legacy platform.","status":"satisfied","summary":"Both nodes remained on Alpine 3.23.3 with kernel 6.18.7-0-lts before and after execution. Alpine-packaged MariaDB 11.4.12 was installed and operated successfully across restarts.","evidence_ids":["global:after_prepare:node1:platform","global:after_prepare:node2:platform","cmd-f4d7b288cca54a52","cmd-5729d4bf4fde4b20","global:after_executor:node1:platform","global:after_executor:node2:platform"]}],"confidence":0.98,"operational_hygiene":{"score":0.9,"summary":"Task-related packages, database configuration, service enablement, accounts, import, and restart operations had clear purposes, and package-health observations did not worsen. Three low-risk hygiene issues remain: cmd-74245bf4597a489d unnecessarily added the cluster key to root's authorized_keys after that approach failed to contribute; it was removed by cmd-a91520baa9e24ea0. Cmd-dc7340a66721447f unnecessarily assigned a password to the temporary public-key transfer account; the account and home were subsequently removed by cmd-a91520baa9e24ea0. The restart commands created /tmp/benchmark-reboot.log on both nodes and left those files behind. No conflicting service or unsafe database bind beyond the managed node1 address was observed.","evidence_ids":["cmd-74245bf4597a489d","cmd-dc7340a66721447f","cmd-a91520baa9e24ea0","cmd-19e9fe7f42c04729","cmd-58a1d176c7b14feb","global:after_executor:node1:temporary-files","global:after_executor:node2:temporary-files","global:after_executor:node1:package-health","global:after_executor:node2:package-health"]},"overall_summary":"All material task outcomes are satisfied. The provider-wide restart protocol was also completed coherently for both nodes: each had a healthy pre-restart state, restart acknowledgement, changed boot identity matching the fixed lifecycle observations, and recovered service or remote access, data, permissions, credentials, and platform state.","limitations":["The lifecycle failed-service probe uses systemd and is unsupported on these Alpine nodes; MariaDB health was nevertheless checked directly with OpenRC and mariadb-admin.","Lifecycle snapshots do not provide a complete filesystem or configuration inventory, so hygiene conclusions outside the captured commands and bounded observations are necessarily limited."]}
